                <pb facs="0458" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.796/280: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reed</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-08-14T19:00:00-04:00">August 14, 1942—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1210. Your 1532, August 7, 6 p.m. and 1553, August 11, 1 p.m. The whole Condor
                    problem has been reviewed with Ambassador Caffery, with whom we have agreed on a
                    formula which he will take up on his return to Brazil.</p>
                <p>Intava should furnish no gasoline to Condor under any circumstances, pending
                    further communication from the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
